WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:16.800
[Music]

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:21.830
[Singing] Who's the guy who fights by keeping
garbage cans clean?

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:26.039
And who's the lucky Joe they picked to
dig the latrine?

00:00:26.039 --> 00:00:29.660
Oh, he's your Uncle's favorite fighting Marine!

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:33.320
McGillicuddy!

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:37.360
Who'd like to get his hands upon that lady
marine?

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:41.920
Who released him for duty in a horse's latrine?

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:46.680
It's that chambermaid commando, that fighting marine,

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:50.140
McGillicuddy! [End of singing]

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:57.420
[Narrator:] But he's not the only one. All the guys have
dirty jobs to do and a smart guy will take

00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:00.870
a bath whenever he can find clean water.

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:04.130
These men want to get the dirt, germs, and
sweat off their skin,

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:06.640
 and a bath is the best method.

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:15.140
But not McGillicuddy! He doesn't like to take
a bath. He's allergic to water.

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:23.300
[Flies are buzzing  around McGillicuddy. A skunk comes out to sniff him but quickly runs away.]

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:33.420
[A silhouetted soldier plays a bugel to awaken the soldiers at sunrise.] 

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:35.540
[McGillicuddy wakes up scratching his body.]

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:42.220
[Narrator:] Uh huh, the first signs of the itch. The skin
you love to scratch.

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:50.380
[McGillicuddy takes off his socks and throws them at the wall, where they stick.]

00:01:51.680 --> 00:02:10.180
[The socks unstick themselves and back away when McGillicuddy tries to grab them; he chases them.]

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:14.640
[McGillicuddy catches his socks after they
surrender in defeat.]

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:26.660
[McGillicuddy's in bed but his feet are covered in rashes and he continuously scratches them.]

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:52.040
[As McGillicuddy sleeps, germs chip and saw away at his feet, making the rash worse.]

00:02:53.160 --> 00:03:01.160
[Bugel plays and soldiers march.]

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:07.260
[Narrator:] Well, McGillicuddy! After a good night's sleep, fresh as a daisy!

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:10.900
[Daisies wilt with McGillicuddy near.]

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:13.360
[Narrator:] Oh, uh, sorry daisies.

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:24.360
[McGillicuddy walks on his hands with feet in the air.]

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:28.120
[Natives pop out from behind trees after McGillicuddy passes.]

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:31.140
[McGillicuddy avoids using his feet; he
swings through the treetops.]

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:37.240
[Natives follow McGillicuddy on the ground.]

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:40.420
[McGillicuddy comes across a sign posted to a tree.]

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:44.160
[Sign is titled Third Commandment: Personal Cleanliness]

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:47.660
[Narrator:] Thou shalt keep thy personal habits clean.

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:57.240
For surely cleanliness is next to Godliness. Dirt and filth are the brothers of discomfort, disease, and death.

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:01.860
[McGillicuddy:] And they ain't kiddin'.

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:08.580
[McGillicuddy's crawling on the ground.]

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:12.100
[McGillicuddy:] Help!

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:16.800
[Natives tie up and carry McGillicuddy away without his shoes.]

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:22.720
[Natives tie McGillicuddy to a tree and stir
a boiling cauldron.]

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:25.680
[Natives hold McGillicuddy above the boiling cauldron.]

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:28.660
[McGillicuddy:] Are, are you gonna eat me?

00:04:29.020 --> 00:04:34.200
[Native, laughing:] No, sir! We're gonna give you a bath!

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:38.000
[Natives drop McGillicuddy into cauldron.]

